index 0000000..aa969e3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/SOLUTION.md
@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+# Solution
+
+Two bugs in `lrucache/cache.py`:
+
+1. **`get` didn't refresh recency.** A successful lookup returned the value but never
+   moved the key to the MRU end of the `OrderedDict`, so a recently-read key could
+   still be picked as the eviction victim. Fixed by calling `move_to_end(key)` before
+   returning.
+
+2. **`put` evicted on updates.** The capacity check ran unconditionally, so overwriting
+   an *existing* key (which doesn't grow the cache) still popped the LRU entry, silently
+   dropping an unrelated key. Fixed by only evicting when the key is new
+   (`key not in self._data and len(...) >= capacity`).
